# gitbackup hard-exclude list.
#
# One glob pattern per line, matched against an absolute path -- either one
# `sysupgrade -l` reported or a directory found while looking for empty
# directories (collect.sh, _gb_collect_is_excluded). "#" starts a comment,
# blank lines are ignored. A pattern ending in "/**" matches the path
# itself and everything under it; anything else is matched with plain
# shell `case` glob rules.
#
# This block is unconditional: it is enforced at every visibility setting.
# The extra secret-file excludes visibility=public adds (/etc/shadow,
# dropbear host keys, uhttpd.key, /etc/ssl/private/**, WireGuard private
# keys -- spec "Scrub") are not here: they depend on a UCI setting this
# file has no way to read, and belong to scrub.sh instead (ticket 05).

# The package's own credentials must never end up inside its own backup,
# no matter how the router is configured (R76).
/etc/gitbackup/**
